# Agent browser: Lightpanda MCP only

Agents drive this app through Lightpanda’s native MCP (`lightpanda mcp`). Lightpanda is already headless and does not paint pixels.

## Do

- Call Lightpanda MCP tools only (`goto`, `tree`, `markdown`, `findElement`, `click`, `fill`, `press`, …).
- Use `http://127.0.0.1:5173` as the app origin (same as Playwright `baseURL`).
- Prefer roles, accessible names, and CSS selectors over hover-only UI and screenshots.

## Do not

- Do not call Playwright MCP (`playwright`, `plugin-playwright-playwright`).
- Do not call Chrome DevTools MCP (`chrome-devtools`).
- Do not run `playwright-cli open`, `playwright-cli attach --cdp`, or any command that launches Chrome for agent browsing.
- Do not open a headed/external GUI browser.

Disable Playwright MCP and Chrome DevTools MCP in Cursor settings so they are not in the tool list. Project MCP can add Lightpanda; it cannot uninstall those plugins.

## Human visual inspection

The Cursor Integrated Browser Tab stays Chromium for the human. Agents must not use it, Playwright MCP, or Chrome DevTools MCP to verify flows.

## Playwright tests

`pnpm test` and `pnpm test:e2e` still launch Chromium. Debugging a paused e2e run with `playwright test --debug=cli` and `playwright-cli attach tw-*` is Chromium and is not agent browsing.
